$$ Read the captured hang with OUR symbols on the path.
$$
$$ The first look resolved every frame in our wrapper to the nearest export,
$$ D3D11CreateDeviceAndSwapChain, which says only "somewhere in d3d11.dll" - and
$$ seventeen threads there is also what an idle sixteen-thread raster pool looks
$$ like. d3d11.pdb sits in the build directory, so put it on the path and let the
$$ frames name themselves before drawing any conclusion.

.sympath F:\rbo_fabre_proto\d3d9_sw;F:\rbo_fabre_proto\d3d9_sw\symbols;srv*F:\rbo_fabre_proto\d3d9_sw\symbols-cache*https://msdl.microsoft.com/download/symbols
.reload /f

.echo ===WHO IS WHERE===
~*k

.echo ===THE LOCK ITSELF===
$$ g_fntabs is a static in d3d11.dll. If the theory holds, its lock word is 1
$$ with no thread able to release it. Printed as a struct-less dump because the
$$ first two LONGs are n and lock.
dq d3d11!g_fntabs L1
.echo ---- records: n, lock, removed, readded, failed, drifted, skipped, unstuck
dd poi(d3d11!g_fntabs) L8

.echo ===DONE===
q
